<article class="env-lemma" id="0AZ4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AZ4">Lemma <span data-tag="0AZ4">10.75.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $M$, $N$ be finite $R$-modules. Then $\text{Tor}_ p^ R(M, N)$ is a finite $R$-module for all $p$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This holds because $\text{Tor}_ p^ R(M, N)$ is computed as the cohomology groups of a complex $F_\bullet \otimes _ R N$ with each $F_ n$ a finite free $R$-module, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00LP" data-tag="00LP">10.71.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>